    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Moseley Shoals is Ocean Colour Scene’s second album and the record that turned the Birmingham band into major Britpop contenders. Released in 1996 on MCA Records, it pairs bright, anthemic guitar rock with a distinctly retro 1960s feel, drawing on mod, soul, and R&B influences to create a warm, muscular sound that set it apart from many of its Britpop peers.\n\nThe album is best known for singles such as “The Riverboat Song,” “The Day We Caught the Train,” and “The Circle,” all of which helped it reach No. 2 on the UK Albums Chart and sustain a long chart run. Widely regarded as the band’s defining statement, Moseley Shoals was praised for its melodic strength and organic production, and it went on to sell more than a million copies worldwide.",
